Generated by `tools/fuelmono-gen.py` from `JS/Interp.lean`; do not edit by hand. `IH H n m` says
that every function of the block that takes fuel, at fuel `n`, is `Le` the same function at
fuel `m`. Each step lemma proves a function's body at `n + 1` against `m + 1` from `IH H n m`,
by walking the two bodies apart (`fuel_mono_pre`, `fuel_call`, `fuel_mono_post`). `IH_all` puts them together:
fuel monotonicity of the whole block, for every heap (the register machine on or off). -/

